WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.969
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.505
we'll deliver slashes
and thrusts

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.806
on this ballistics dummy.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.040
Collin, you're up first.
You ready?

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.475
-Have fun.
-Let's do this.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.778
To help me today,
I'm bringing back

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.180
one of Marcaida Kali's
chief instructors.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.217
Please welcome U.S.
Staff Sergeant Chris Manns.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.022
[dramatic rock music plays]

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.047
All right, Collin, your
Kabyle flyssa is very sharp.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:50.816
On the initial thrust, it
penetrated deep and easily

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.818
through this whole
ballistics dummy.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.053
The handle is comfortable.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:56.856
It's easy to slash
in and thrust out.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.558
Overall, it will kill.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:00.626
Good job.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.061
Thank you, sir.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.429
Daniel, your turn.
You ready?

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.430
Yes, sir.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.168
[dramatic rock music plays]

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.218
[man laughs] Oh man.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.594
All right, Daniel, your weapon
is wicked sharp.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.596
On the initial thrust,
it penetrated deep.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.765
And on the way out,
with your belly being forward,

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.868
it lacerates out easily.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:46.072
Now, because you have such a
very skinny handle right here

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.273
and there is no pommel
with a counterweight,

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.276
all the weight is in front.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.845
The balance just
makes the blade rotate

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:54.580
with a small handle like this.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.017
But in terms of damage,
it will kill.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.618
-Thank you.
-Good job.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:02.222
All right, bladesmiths.
Next up is the strength test.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.523
Ben?

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.625
Bladesmiths, to test
the strength and durability

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.895
of your Kabyle flyssa,
I'll be smashing them

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.630
into these
terracotta pots, edge first.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.999
Remember, this test is all about
what the pots do to your blades,

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.834
and not what the blades do
to the pots.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.168
Collin, you're up first. Ready?

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.570
-Yes, sir.
-All right.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:21.340
[dramatic music plays]

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:25.278
[dramatic rock music plays]

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.283
-Awesome, man.
-[Collin sighs]

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.087
Collin, your blade
held up beautifully.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:36.622
The, uh, edge

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.391
looks like it never saw
the terracotta.

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:40.559
-Did a great job. Well done.
-Thank you, sir.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.995
-Daniel, you're up. Ready?
-I'm ready.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.098
[dramatic musical sting]

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:49.369
[dramatic rock music plays]

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:59.645
[tense music plays]

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.247
Well, Daniel, your edge held up
pretty well.

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:03.549
If I run my fingers across,

00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:06.085
I can feel just a little bit
of a wire edge.

00:03:06.151 --> 00:03:07.620
But nothing major.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.122
But my big concern...

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.890
This handle.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.728
It's so small that I had
a tough time indexing it.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.297
But it's beautifully carved.
Edge held up beautifully.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.866
-Very well done.
-Thank you, sir.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.136
All right, gentlemen,
you survived our kill test

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.271
and our strength test.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.106
Now the sharpness test.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:28.373
To test the sharpness
of that blade

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.009
and to see if it
still has an edge,

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.944
I'll be cutting
through these fish.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:35.381
A clean, sharp blade should
pass right through those fish.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:38.250
A dull blade is gonna knock
those fish out of the way

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.085
or give us a jagged, torn cut.

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:41.821
-Collin, you ready?
-Yes, sir.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.122
-Okay.
-<i> And I'm just thinking,</i>

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.024
please just slice
through this thing.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:48.494
[dramatic music plays]

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:11.050
All right, Collin, right off,
it's definitely a sharp blade.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.217
It cut very nicely.

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:15.955
Your handle is a bit
on the fat side.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.457
But it's definitely a cutter.
Good job.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.693
-Thank you, sir.
-Daniel, are you ready?-

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:21.994
-Yes.
-Okay, great.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:25.131
I feel that Collin and I
are still neck and neck.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.232
<i> I think that I've got
 a good edge on him.</i>

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:31.271
[dramatic music plays]

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:38.778
-[grunts]
-[Daniel] Hm.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.750
All right, Daniel,
this blade is wicked sharp.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.486
And those cuts.
You can see, they just

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.054
blew right through the fish.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:53.059
My problem is,
this is so small,

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.295
I had to fight to keep it
in my hand.

00:04:56.728 --> 00:05:00.632
These flyssa often have
a very small handle.

00:05:00.732 --> 00:05:03.235
But what saves that
is having that pommel

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.837
keeping your hand
from coming off

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.439
the back of that blade.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.607
It's an amazing cutter.

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:11.844
It's just very difficult
to hold onto.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.049
[Wil] Daniel, Collin,
there can only be

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.684
one<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion.

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:20.586
And that champion is...

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:26.859
Collin.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:27.760
Congratulations,

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.762
you are our new
<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.531
Daniel, your sword
didn't make the cut.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.567
Please surrender your blade.

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.570
[Daniel]<i> I am disappointed
 that I didn't win.</i>

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.340
But I'm absolutely proud
of the work I did here.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:43.342
If anything, I think this fuels
my fire to work harder

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.877
<i> and do better.</i>

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.113
Collin, congratulations.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.881
You are our new
<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.116
That's a title that comes
with a check for ten grand.

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.517
-Good job, buddy.
-[applause]

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.020
As far as your animal head
pommel,

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:57.522
I'm gonna go ahead and say
it's probably an underdog.

00:05:57.622 --> 00:05:59.391
-[laughter]
-Well, Collin,

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:02.662
please present your weapon
to the judges.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:07.767
[Collin]<i> Wil Willis out here
 telling me I'm a champion?</i>

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.702
Can you believe it?!

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.003
[grunts gleefully]

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:14.072
<i> Champ! I can't believe it!</i>

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:16.876
<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion
out here.

00:06:18.076 --> 00:06:20.045
[groans joyfully]

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:23.383
[dramatic music plays]

